id: ai-developer
name: AI Developer Workflow
version: 1
description: |
  Phase 1 Router Migration Pipeline
  - Ticket Picker: Auto-select next Linear ticket from backlog
  - Developer: Generate + fix router code with MiniMax-M2.5
  - Auditor: Pre-review with DeepSeek (security + best practices)
  - Reviewer: Final Claude code review
  - Auto-merge cron monitors and merges when approved

polling:
  model: anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
  timeoutSeconds: 180

agents:
  - id: ticket_picker
    name: Ticket Picker
    role: analysis
    model: anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
    description: Auto-picks next ready Linear ticket from Phase 1 backlog
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/ticket_picker
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/ticket_picker/AGENTS.md

  - id: developer
    name: Developer
    role: coding
    model: minimax-portal/MiniMax-M2.5
    description: Generates router code with MiniMax-M2.5, applies fixes
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/developer
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/developer/AGENTS.md

  - id: auditor
    name: Auditor (DeepSeek)
    role: analysis
    model: deepseek/deepseek-chat
    description: Pre-reviews code for security + performance before PR
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/auditor
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/auditor/AGENTS.md

  - id: closer
    name: Closer
    role: analysis
    model: anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
    description: Monitors PR status, handles post-merge cleanup
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/closer
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/closer/AGENTS.md

steps:
  - id: pick_ticket
    agent: ticket_picker
    input: |
      Pick the next ready ticket from Phase 1 of AMA-583 refactoring.

      Phase 1 backlog (STRICT ORDER - do not skip):
      1. AMA-588: Follow-along integration tests (✅ DONE - merged)
      2. AMA-592: Bulk import integration tests (IN PROGRESS)
      3. AMA-593: Programs router
      4. AMA-594: Tags router
      5. AMA-595: Unit tests for programs + tags routers
      6. AMA-596: Account router
      7. AMA-598: Unit tests for account router
      8. AMA-597: Move debug endpoints to health router
      9. AMA-599: Verify app.py is empty and clean up
      10. AMA-600: Create ExportService layer
      11. AMA-601: Unit tests for ExportService
      12. AMA-602: Implement async export queue
      13. AMA-603: Unit tests for async export queue
      14. AMA-605: Final integration tests (MUST BE LAST)

      Task (CRITICAL - FOLLOW EXACT ORDER):
      1. Pick the NEXT ticket in the sequence above that hasn't been merged yet
      2. Start with AMA-592 (bulk import tests) if this is the first run
      3. Check Linear for ticket status, description, acceptance criteria
      4. Verify all dependencies from previous steps are merged
      5. Do NOT skip ahead or pick out of order
      6. If a ticket is done, move to the next one in sequence

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      TICKET_ID: AMA-XXX
      TITLE: What the ticket is about
      DESCRIPTION: Full description from Linear
      ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA: |
        - Criterion 1
        - Criterion 2
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    max_retries: 1
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human

  - id: develop
    agent: developer
    model: anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
    timeoutSeconds: 120
    input: |
      Generate and implement {{ticket_id}} ({{title}}).

      TICKET: {{ticket_id}}
      TITLE: {{title}}
      DESCRIPTION: {{description}}
      ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA:
      {{acceptance_criteria}}

      Instructions:
      1. Read examples: api/routers/settings.py, api/routers/follow_along.py, api/routers/sync.py
      2. Create api/routers/[new_router].py with same patterns
      3. Wire into backend/main.py _include_routers()
      4. Create feature branch: git checkout -b feature/{{ticket_id}}-short-name
      5. Commit and push
      6. Create PR to main with ticket ID in title

      Use MiniMax-M2.5 for all code generation (highest quality).

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      ROUTER_FILE: api/routers/...
      PR_NUMBER: #NNN
      PR_URL: https://github.com/...
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    max_retries: 2
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human

  - id: audit
    agent: auditor
    input: |
      Pre-review {{router_file}} for security + best practices.

      ROUTER: {{router_file}}
      TICKET: {{ticket_id}}
      PR: {{pr_url}}

      Task:
      1. Use DeepSeek to search:
         - "FastAPI router best practices 2025"
         - "OWASP top 10 FastAPI vulnerabilities"
         - "Pydantic validation patterns"
      2. Read the generated router code
      3. Check for:
         - Missing authentication (all endpoints need user dependency)
         - Missing input validation (Pydantic models, Field constraints)
         - Error handling (specific exceptions, not bare Exception)
         - Type safety (proper return types, enums)
         - Security (no credential leaks, SQL injection risks)
         - Performance (no N+1, blocking calls, etc.)
      4. Generate audit report with specific line numbers
      5. If issues found, output them for developer to fix

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      AUDIT_RESULT: pass|fail
      ISSUES: (if any)
        - Issue 1 (line XXX)
        - Issue 2 (line YYY)
      RECOMMENDATIONS:
        - Fix 1
        - Fix 2

      Or if critical issues:
      STATUS: escalate
      CRITICAL_ISSUES:
        - Blocker 1
        - Blocker 2
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    on_fail:
      retry_step: develop
      max_retries: 1

  - id: wait_review
    agent: closer
    input: |
      Monitor PR {{pr_number}} for Claude code review approval.

      PR: {{pr_number}}
      URL: {{pr_url}}

      Task:
      1. Wait for Claude code review to complete
      2. If approved: reply with STATUS: approved
      3. If changes requested: wait for developer to fix (they'll push updates)
      4. Check every 30 seconds for up to 5 minutes

      The auto-merge cron job will handle the actual merge.

      Reply with:
      STATUS: approved
      TIMESTAMP: when approved
    expects: "STATUS: approved"
    max_retries: 10
    retry_delay: 30
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human

  - id: post_merge
    agent: closer
    input: |
      {{ticket_id}} PR #{{pr_number}} has been merged. Mark ticket complete.

      TICKET: {{ticket_id}}
      PR: {{pr_number}}

      Task:
      1. In Linear, move {{ticket_id}} to "Done"
      2. Log completion in MEMORY.md
      3. Next iteration will pick up the next ticket

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      TICKET: {{ticket_id}}
      NEXT: auto-pick next ticket
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human

steps_flow:
  - pick_ticket
  - develop
  - audit
  - wait_review
  - post_merge
